  "chapter": 201,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                 APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 4 Chapter 201\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7503-B, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to requiring\n        retailers  of  micromobility  devices,  bicycles  with  electric\n        assist  and  limited  use  motorcycles  powered  by  lithium-ion\n        batteries, and lithium-ion batteries intended for  use  in  such\n        devices or bicycles to provide customers with an operating manu-\n        al\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  prohibit  the  sale  or  offer  for sale of certain\ndevices, including bicycles with electric assist, limited  use  motorcy-\ncles  and  micromobility devices, without an operating manual containing\ninstructions on how to store and charge the battery as well as  what  to\ndo  if  the  battery overheats, emits a strange odor or changes shape or\ncolor.\n \n  I strongly support the intent of this bill to enhance consumer  safety\nby  making important information readily available to New Yorkers. These\nkinds of devices often rely  on  lithium-ion  batteries  that  may  pose\nunique  fire hazards. Providing safety information along with the device\nitself makes the information easily accessible and will help to  prevent\nlithium-ion battery fires. I have secured an agreement with the Legisla-\nture  to clarify that such devices may not be manufactured, distributed,\nreconditioned, assembled, sold or offered for sale without such an oper-\nating manual as well as an agreement to make technical changes,  includ-\ning  harmonizing  certain  definitions  with  other  New  York  laws for\nconsistency. Based upon this agreement, I am pleased to sign  this  bill\ninto law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2024
 },
